From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:13:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): settle queued !cmd bubbles a reconnect recovers

A `!cmd` sent to a claude-native or codex-native session gets no
session.input.consumed receipt. Its queued bubble clears only when the
live terminal_command item event arrives. If the stream drops while the
command waits or runs (a phone locks, a laptop sleeps, the proxy recycles
the connection), that event fires into the dead socket. The reconnect
backfill then splices the committed terminal_command item into the
transcript, but it only acknowledges recovered user messages, so the
bubble stays pinned to the bottom of the chat until a full reload.

Settle the bubbles of recovered shell inputs on both reconnect paths,
the incremental backfill and the fresh-window fallback, using the same
command match and per-item dedupe as the live handler, which now shares
the helper. Shell bubbles are settled before the user-message FIFO
acknowledgement, so that count no longer lands on a shell bubble.

Not upstream yet: proposed from fix/web-reconnect-settles-shell-inputs; drop this copy once it
merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit d7962b0eb7ce60a7160e2704472f88c045e7922e)
Docs: none (fix: queued !cmd bubbles settle after a reconnect; no setting)
---
